{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Provide for yourselves.</b> Prepare yourselves for the matter." "<b>Men.</b> Now would it even occur to you — women? So what does אֲנָשִׁים tell you? Righteous men, as in ״כְּסוּפִים״." "<b>Wise and discerning.</b> Understanding one thing from within another. That is what Arius asked Rabbi Yose: What is the difference between חֲכָמִים and נְבוֹנִים? A חָכָם is like a wealthy money-changer: when they bring him dinars to examine, he examines, but when they do not bring him, he sits idle. A נָבוֹן is like a merchant money-changer: when they bring him coins to examine, he examines, and when they do not bring him, he goes around and brings from his own (Sifrei)." "<b>And known to your tribes.</b> That they are recognized by you — for if one comes before me wrapped in his tallit, I do not know who he is or from which tribe he is, and whether he is fit. But you recognize him, for you raised him. Therefore it says וִידֻעִים לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶם (Sifrei)." "<b>As heads over you.</b> Chiefs and honored by you — that you should treat them with honor and awe." "<b>ואשמם.</b> Defective in yod — teaching that the guilt of Israel hangs upon the heads of their judges, for it was theirs to rebuke and direct them to the straight path (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:29.938972521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}